Two blocks slide directly towards each other along a frictionless horizontal surface, as shown in Fig. 4.1. The blocks collide and then move as shown in Fig. 4.2.

{{figure:figure_4_1}}

{{figure:figure_4_2}}

Block X initially moves to the right with a momentum of $0.37\text{ kg m s}^{-1}$. Block Y initially moves to the left with a momentum of $0.65\text{ kg m s}^{-1}$. After the blocks collide, block X moves to the left back along its original path with a momentum of $0.13\text{ kg m s}^{-1}$. Block Y also moves to the left after the collision.

